{"id":"18a544cc-63ca-42e9-ad80-c6e5cb0827c7","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a4eb2d27eddc588a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/tasks.ts","baseline":{"blob":"feb110e850e58c2302109e0face383ecfa3e21db","start":0,"end":46},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Hub","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/hub","\""]},"context":{"after":"2c1cb6475bc215a0"}},"payload":{"text":"Every package.json script is a task (RUNNING.md, *The model*): in VS Code's Run Task and in the shell's Run menu\n(shell/run-menu.tsx), each run by the workspace's terminal in a terminal of its own, ending when the script does and with its\nexit code. `npm run` there is what runs it, so a dev server's a service like any other (workbench/runs.ts).\n\n`tasks.list`: each script, and whether it's up already. `tasks.run`: a script, unless it's a service that's up: then its\npreview's shown, rather than a second copy started. `tasks.runFile`: the file in sight (extensions/tsval/run-file.ts).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:48.337Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:48.337Z"}
